    "result": {
        "response": "The study has two primary endpoints:\n\n### 1. Primary Efficacy Endpoint\n**Clinical and endoscopic remission at Week 12**, defined as:\n- Full Mayo score \u2264 2\n- No individual subscore > 1\n- Rectal bleeding subscore = 0\n\nThis is a binary outcome (remission status = yes/no) analyzed using a **logistic regression model** with treatment and randomisation-stratification factors (prior corticosteroids treatment and consent to participate in PK substudy) as fixed effects, and baseline full Mayo score as a covariate. Patients with missing remission status data are assumed to **not be in remission**. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 68; p. 7; p. 30)\n\nThe **full Mayo score** (range 0\u201312; higher score = worse) is based on the clinician's scoring of clinical signs and symptoms, as well as endoscopic scoring of gross colonic mucosal inflammation. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 30)\n\n### 2. Primary Safety Endpoint\n- **Adverse events**\n- **Vital signs**\n- **12-lead Electrocardiography (ECG)**\n- **Clinical safety laboratory abnormalities**\n\n(Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 7)",
